[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:111. The Most Expensive Model]
[00:01.961]Lesson 111 | 第111课
[00:04.370]I like this record player very much. | 我非常喜欢这台电唱机。
[00:08.125]How much does it cost, please? | 请问它多少钱？
[00:10.680]It's the most expensive model in the shop. | 这是店里最贵的一款。
[00:13.905]It costs 64 pounds. | 它要64英镑。
[00:16.620]That's too expensive for us. | 对我们来说太贵了。
[00:19.565]We can't afford all that money. | 我们付不起那么多钱。
[00:23.005]This model's less expensive than that one. | 这款不如那款贵。
[00:27.045]It's only 28 pounds. | 它只要28英镑。
[00:30.050]But of course, it's not as good as the expensive one. | 当然，它不如那款贵的质量好。
[00:34.625]I don't like this model. | 我不喜欢这一款。
[00:37.385]The other model's more expensive, but it's worth the money. | 另一款更贵，但它物有所值。
[00:43.210]Can we buy it on installments? | 我们可以分期付款购买吗？
[00:46.335]Of course. | 当然。
[00:47.515]You can pay a deposit of 10 pounds and then 1 pound a week for 60 weeks. | 你可以先付10英镑的押金，然后每周付1英镑，分60周付清。
[00:53.880]Do you like it, dear? | 亲爱的，你喜欢它吗？
[00:55.635]I certainly do, but I don't like the price. | 我当然喜欢，但我不喜欢它的价格。
[00:59.845]You always want the best, but we can't afford it. | 你总是想要最好的，但我们付不起。
[01:04.120]Sometimes you think you're a millionaire. | 有时候你以为你是个百万富翁。
[01:07.275]Millionaires don't buy things on installments. | 百万富翁不会分期付款购物的。